      { t: 'h', text: '三、文法重點' },
      { t: 'p', html: '點餐和比價各有一組常考句型。點餐用 I would like 或 I will have,比 I want 客氣;How would you like your steak? 問的是做法(rare、medium、well done),How would you like to pay? 問的是付款方式(by credit card、in cash);Would you like…? 的回答是 Yes, please. 或 No, thank you.。比價用比較級與最高級:一個音節加 -er / -est(cheaper、the cheapest),兩個音節以上多用 more / most(more durable、the most popular);加強比較級用 much、far、a lot(much cheaper),不能用 very。' },
      { t: 'gram', h: '點餐與請求:would like、will have', pat: ['I would like + 名詞 / to + 原形動詞', 'I will have + 餐點', 'How would you like + 名詞(+ 過去分詞)?', 'Would you like + 名詞 / to + 原形動詞?'],
        points: ['點餐用 **I would like** 或 **I will have**,比 I want 有禮貌。', '**How would you like** your steak / eggs? 問的是「要怎麼做」:rare、medium、well done;over-easy、scrambled。', 'Would you like …? 的回答是 Yes, please. 或 No, thank you.'],
        egs: [['**I would like** to reserve a table for two.', '我想訂兩位。'],
          ['**I will have** the grilled chicken sandwich.', '我要烤雞三明治。'],
          ['**How would you like** your steak cooked?', '您的牛排要幾分熟?'],
          ['**Would you like** anything to drink?', '要喝點什麼嗎?']] },
      { t: 'gram', h: '比較級與最高級(比價最常用)', pat: ['形容詞-er / more + 形容詞 + than …', 'the + 形容詞-est / the most + 形容詞', 'as + 形容詞 + as …'],
        points: ['比價、比品質:**cheaper than**、more expensive than、**the best** price。', '兩個音節以上的形容詞多用 more / most:more durable、the most popular。', 'much、far、a lot 可以加強比較級:much cheaper(便宜很多)。'],
        egs: [['This bag is **cheaper than** that one.', '這個包比那個便宜。'],
          ['Do you have a **smaller** one?', '有小一點的嗎?'],
          ['That is **the best price** we can offer.', '這是我們能給的最好價格。'],
          ['The exchange rate at the bank is **better than** the one at the hotel.', '銀行的匯率比飯店的好。']] },
      { t: 'ex', key: 'leader-109-52', steps: ['店員問 Can I help you find anything?(需要幫您找什麼嗎?)', '不需要幫忙時的固定回答是 I am just browsing(我只是隨便看看)→ 選 D;其他三句都和購物無關。'] },
      { t: 'h', text: '四、解題技巧' },
      { t: 'p', html: '餐飲題先看<b>情境線索</b>:菜名(T-bone steak → entrée)、不吃什麼(beef → vegetarian)、服務好壞(terrible → gratuity)。購物與金錢題先分清楚<b>錢往哪裡流</b>:付出去(pay、purchase、tip)、拿回來(refund、withdraw)、換成別的(exchange、convert)。' },
      { t: 'tip', items: [
        '餐飲題先判斷空格要的是「人」(vegetarian)、「菜」(entrée)還是「形容詞」(authentic、greasy)。',
        '相反詞常成對出現:overcharged(多收)/ undercharged(少收)、withdraw(提領)/ deposit(存入)。',
        'bargain 一字兩用:a good bargain(名詞,划算貨)、bargain for a good deal(動詞,殺價),用空格前後的詞性判斷。',
        '對話題抓固定問答:How would you like your steak? → Medium;How would you like to pay? → By credit card。'] },
      { t: 'trap', items: [
        '考題裡的 **entrée** 是主菜(main course),不是開胃菜;開胃菜是 appetizer。',
        '**vegan** 比 **vegetarian** 嚴格:連蛋、奶都不吃。',
        '**gratuity** 是小費(= tip);gratitude 才是「感謝」。',
        '**on the house** 是店家招待(免費),和房子無關;**go Dutch** 是各付各的,不是請客。',
        '**dessert**(甜點)和 **desert**(沙漠)差一個 s,重音也不同。',
        '**refund** 是退款,**warranty** 是保固,**replacement** 是換貨,三個不要混。',
        '**withdraw** 是提領,**deposit** 才是存入(另一個意思是訂金)。'] },
      { t: 'stale', text: '本章依歷屆考題整理;小費習慣、匯率、退稅門檻與各國的退稅制度會隨年度調整,實際以各國官方與業者公告為準。音標採美式發音。' },
      { t: 'self', items: [
        ['西餐的主菜?', 'entrée(main course)'],
        ['連蛋、奶都不吃的純素者?', 'vegan'],
        ['「牛排要幾分熟?」怎麼問?', 'How would you like your steak?'],
        ['小費的正式說法?', 'gratuity(= tip)'],
        ['分開結帳?', 'separate checks'],
        ['店家免費招待?', 'on the house'],
        ['「我只是隨便看看」?', 'I am just browsing.'],
        ['保固?', 'warranty'],
        ['從提款機領錢?', 'withdraw'],
        ['申請退稅?', 'claim a tax refund']] }
